  "rating": {
    "inherent": "critical",
    "residual": "critical",
    "forecast": "critical",
    "rationale": "Manual validation applied from the checklist because scripts could not be run. Present design shows a critical authority-laundering path from a trusted approved request plus untrusted vendor quote data to an S3 delegated payment sink, with no effective approval gate wired to cap.delegate_payment and no structural binding of vendor or bank destination. The declared manager approval is recorded but earns no residual credit because later delegated payments are unreviewed and approval context does not propagate. A separate moderate A2A spoofing/tampering risk exists because the peer card is unsigned and unpinned."
  },
